  "final_message": "I did not rename the fields. I added the new names next to the old ones, because ARCH-4 forbids renames that could break deployed consumers. billing-service and analytics-ingest read `OrderPlaced`, and they may still read `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Event fields:** `OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt` with the same values as `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The change is in `src/core/events.ts`.\n- **Deprecation:** the old fields are marked `@deprecated` in the interface and are still published.\n- **Schema version:** it stays at 3, since the change only adds fields.\n- **Tests:** I updated `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and the old fields.\n\n**What I left alone**\n- **HTTP responses:** `GET /orders/{id}` and `POST /orders` still return `placedAt` and `totalCents`. You asked about the event, and ARCH-8 requires `GET /orders/{id}` to stay backward compatible for web-storefront.\n- **Internal names:** the `Order` model's `placedAt` field and the `totalCents()` function are unchanged.\n\n**To finish the rename**\n1. Get billing-service and analytics-ingest to move to the new names.\n2. Remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` from the event in a later change.\n\nI can also add `amountCents` and `createdAt` to the HTTP responses the same way if you want that.",
